# Flutter mobile rules

## Ownership and PR control

- Only Omar may merge, close, mark ready, auto-merge, change the PR target, or
  delete the working branch.
- Keep PRs draft/open unless Omar explicitly instructs otherwise.
- Do not create a replacement PR for an existing reviewable PR unless Omar
  explicitly requests that.

## Architecture and API

- Laravel `origin/staging` `docs/api/v1/openapi.yaml` is the API source of truth.
- Keep code feature-first, testable, and understandable without generic clean
  architecture boilerplate.
- Use Riverpod and go_router without code generation.
- Keep one configured Dio client. Never log auth request/response data.
- Keep bearer tokens only in the `TokenStorage` secure-storage abstraction.
- Persist access token and expiry together as one atomic secure-storage value.
- Never persist username/password, authenticator/recovery codes, or 2FA
  challenges.
- Clear local auth on authoritative rejection, not on timeout/offline/5xx.
- Clear tokens only for the request session that observed unauthorized
  responses.
- Do not decide 2FA expiry on the client clock; let the API own challenge
  validity.
- Never surface raw API `message` or unknown `code` values in UI.
- Put all user-facing strings in ARB files and maintain Arabic/English parity.
- Preserve Android namespace and application ID `tr.indirimgo.app`.
- Main/release Android must deny cleartext; only debug may allow local HTTP for
  `10.0.2.2`, `127.0.0.1`, and `localhost`.
- Keep Android backup disabled while tokens live in app-private secure storage.
- Pin CI Flutter/Dart versions; do not float on `channel: stable` without an
  exact version.
- Flutter must never calculate trusted prices or mutate financial state
  independently of Laravel.
- Do not add biometric unlock, refresh tokens, deep links, push, maps, media
  upload, or other deferred features during M1.2.
- Do not claim production-signing readiness from debug APK success alone.
